/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 106 0 R
/T (Interpretation: Under default FIFO queueing \(Run 3\), greedy TCP file downloads fill the router's outbound buffer \(bufferbloat\), forcing small 200-byte VoIP packets to wait behind 1,500-byte data frames and causing severe jitter and tail drops. Enabling Low-Latency Queueing \(LLQ / strict priority for DSCP EF voice in Run 4\) schedules voice packets ahead of bulk TCP transfers, restoring crystal-clear audio while TCP gracefully scales back to the remaining 1.12 Mbps.)
/E (Interpretation: Under default FIFO queueing \(Run 3\), greedy TCP file downloads fill the router's outbound buffer \(bufferbloat\), forcing small 200-byte VoIP packets to wait behind 1,500-byte data frames and causing severe jitter and tail drops. Enabling Low-Latency Queueing \(LLQ / strict priority for DSCP EF voice in Run 4\) schedules voice packets ahead of bulk TCP transfers, restoring crystal-clear audio while TCP gracefully scales back to the remaining 1.12 Mbps.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
