/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 109 0 R
/T (Per-source-IP rate limits \(e.g., 25 req/s per student IP\) scale linearly with user count because each new student has a distinct IP address. However, if a regional centre or college campus sits behind a single shared NAT IP, doubling users could trigger false-positive rate-limit blocks; therefore, rate limits must be keyed per authenticated session token/user ID at the WAF/reverse- proxy layer and stateful connection table max-entries doubled \(e.g., from 65,536 to 131,072\).)
/E (Per-source-IP rate limits \(e.g., 25 req/s per student IP\) scale linearly with user count because each new student has a distinct IP address. However, if a regional centre or college campus sits behind a single shared NAT IP, doubling users could trigger false-positive rate-limit blocks; therefore, rate limits must be keyed per authenticated session token/user ID at the WAF/reverse- proxy layer and stateful connection table max-entries doubled \(e.g., from 65,536 to 131,072\).)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [15]
>>
